    "ms_faq": {
      "type": "ms-faq",
      "name": "Questions and answers",
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where are Midsummer beds made?",
            "answer": "<p>By hand in Italy. Every sleep system is built one by one by two artisans, start to finish — the same two hands that open the spring core sew the final seam.</p>",
            "open": true
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can a bed be made to my dimensions?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Dimensions, heights, fibres, fabric and comfort level are specification decisions rather than exceptions. Non-standard widths, heights and radii, including round, carry no tooling charge.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which natural materials do you use?",
            "answer": "<p>Baby alpaca, Cheviot wool, horsehair, vegetable horsehair, yak hair, mohair, cashmere, silk, linen, organic cotton and Orange Fiber. Vicuña is used in the Icons collection. Systems are upholstered in Loro Piana Interiors fabrics.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the 15 + 15 service?",
            "answer": "<p>Our regeneration service. At year fifteen the mattress returns to the Italian artisans who made it, and its comfort, integrity and life are restored for the fifteen years ahead, rather than the system being replaced.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why are prices not shown?",
            "answer": "<p>Because every system is made to order, and the price follows the specification: dimensions, height, fibres, fabric and comfort level. We quote after the consultation. Price on request.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do the three collections differ?",
            "answer": "<p>Essentials is the entry point — five systems, natural fibres, authentic artisan construction. Signature is the heart of the collection — seven systems in Loro Piana Interiors fabrics over spring architectures built for the highest comfort. Icons is the most important work we do — twelve systems, six layers of springs, vicuña and cashmere, fully upholstered.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I try a bed before ordering?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Come and lie down at the atelier, Via Andegari 4, Milano, Monday to Friday, 09:00–12:00 and 13:00–18:00. We can also meet by video. Appointments are confirmed by email within one working day.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you work with architects and interior designers?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The project desk issues drawings, sections and material schedules for your set, gives access to the full Loro Piana Interiors palette with COM on request, and applies professional pricing, staged payments and white-glove installation.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you supply hotels and contract projects?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We supply hotels, branded residences and yachts with phased production aligned to floor handovers, fire-retardancy and contract certification prepared per market, housekeeping protocols per system, and the 15 + 15 service written into the agreement.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does delivery take?",
            "answer": "<p>Production and delivery windows are confirmed on enquiry, because each system is made to order. Delivery is white-glove: the bed is brought into the room, assembled and dressed by our own team.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "qa_11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I care for the system?",
            "answer": "<p>Rotate head to foot every three months for the first year, then twice yearly. Air the system when you change the linen. Loro Piana Interiors upholstery should be dry-cleaned by a specialist only; the atelier can arrange this.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "qa_1",
        "qa_2",
        "qa_3",
